This applies only to the files authored in this repository. Third-party dependencies
carry their own licences and are unaffected -- in particular the OpenZeppelin contracts,
which are MIT and remain so, and which appear as separate files with their own SPDX
headers wherever this project's contracts are verified on a block explorer.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note for anyone reading this on a block explorer:

Block explorers classify licences from a fixed list. "UNLICENSED" is not on it, and the
nearest-sounding entry -- "The Unlicense" -- is a PUBLIC DOMAIN DEDICATION and the
opposite of what this file says. Where a licence field is shown for these contracts it
is set to "none", which is the only value on that list consistent with the above.
